   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "**MOSS-Image SFT banding fix: presets**\n\nPick a preset above; it sets the LoRA strengths and step count for you.\n\n- **Quality**: banding-fix LoRA, 25 steps. Closest to SFT, stripes gone.\n- **Quality+**: also reverts layers 32-36. Cleanest, slightly different look.\n- **Balanced / Fast / Fast alt**: fix + a speed LoRA at partial strength, 14 / 10 steps.\n- **Off**: plain SFT, to compare.\n- **Turbo / Turbo max**: rapid-moss nodes, 8 / 4 steps, very fast; recomposes more. Keep **Width x Height near 1 MP** (1024x1024, 1216x832, 832x1216): the adapters were trained there, and bigger sizes break into a grid of repeated tiny subjects, worse with short prompts. Write detailed prompts. For bigger images use Fast or Balanced.\n- **Turbo hi-res (experimental)**: Turbo max at ~1 MP, latent upscale to your size, then 3 Fast steps at 0.5 denoise. About twice as fast as Fast at big sizes (~6 s vs ~11 s at 1664x1136 on a 5090), but these settings don't hold up every time: detailed photo areas such as foliage get a canvas-like texture, and Turbo's odd choices (extra props, sloppy distant figures, misspelled text) carry over. Usually not worth it, but not fully tuned either: stage-2 steps, denoise and upscale method are a starting point if you want to experiment.\n\nLoRAs at strength 0 are skipped, but the files must exist (see the model card)."
   ],
   "title": "How to use"
  },
